    "note": "Original post did not expose a complete repeatable prompt. Treat this as a source-linked Figma Motion reference.",
    "originalText": "Just tried the AI agent for motion in @figma \n\nAs expected, it's far from great\n\nBut it's not completely useless\n\nIt can do simple slideshows, mass update keyframes, easing, etc\n\nGood way to eliminate repetitive work\n\nThis is the prompt i used btw:\n\nShowcase animation: move the group to reveal each child frame one at a time, centered in the viewport. Jump between frames in a non-sequential order so the camera feels like it's exploring, no row-by-row pattern. Use smooth, human-like panning: gentle ease-in out of rest, long deceleration into each stop (cubic bezier ~0.4, 0, 0.2, 1). Hold each frame briefly before moving on. At the end, pan back to the first frame so the animation loops seamlessly",
